<!--MachineBlocks MBOM — preset catalog for one target Block

  FQN: com.machineblocks.bml.core.BlockPresets
  Abstract — a concrete catalog extends BlockPresets and closes T.-->
<mbcore:BlockPresets xmlns="http://blockml.org/bml"
  xmlns:bricks="com.machineblocks.bml.bricks"
  xmlns:mbcore="com.machineblocks.bml.core"
  xmlns:scad="com.machineblocks.bml.documentation.scad">

  <baseType>
    mbcore:Block
  </baseType>
  <is>
    A preset catalog for one target Block
  </is>
  <documentation>
    Abstract preset catalog. Open generic T (baseType Block) is the target block these
    presets apply to. A concrete catalog extends BlockPresets and closes T with that
    target, for example BlockPresets(bricks:Standard). presets is then T[].

    Each presets entry is a named, partial instance of T. basePresets stays on Block
    and resolves sibling entries in this composition by bml:id. Preset merge walks
    basePresets in order: a later base overrides an earlier one on the same property,
    then the entry's own literals override the bases. A cycle is an error.

    The machineblocks-v3-scad target recognizes a closed BlockPresets(T) and writes
    customizer JSON { fileFormatVersion: "1", parameterSets }. The file name is the
    manifestation of T with extension .json, beside T's .scad file, so OpenSCAD loads
    it. The catalog block's own FQN is not the output name. Each parameter set omits
    name, basePresets, values equal to T's literal default, and values that do not
    serialize. Strings are stored unquoted; numbers and booleans are stored as text;
    a SizeXYZ value is stored as [x, y, z].
  </documentation>
  <abstract>
    true
  </abstract>
  <references>
    <see type="mbcore:Block">
      Domain base. basePresets stays on Block; the presets aggregation does not.
    </see>
    <see type="scad:BlockFileStructure" relation="SeeAlso">
      Customizer JSON is written under the manifestation filename of T.
    </see>
    <see type="bricks:StandardPresets" relation="SeeAlso">
      Concrete catalog — BlockPresets(Standard) for the Standard brick.
    </see>
  </references>
  <genericTypes>
    <T baseType="mbcore:Block">
      <documentation>
        Target block these presets apply to. A concrete catalog binds T in baseType.
        presets is a collection of that type. The customizer JSON uses T's
        manifestation filename.
      </documentation>
    </T>
  </genericTypes>
  <aggregations>
    <presets type="T[]">
      <documentation>
        Named preset instances of T. basePresets on an entry references other entries
        in this composition by bml:id.
      </documentation>
    </presets>
  </aggregations>
</mbcore:BlockPresets>
